00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.829 align:start position:0%
 
you're looking at the beautiful augusta  national golf club home of the masters  where this year's tournament is  officially underway this morning  [Music]  a short time ago gary player and jack  nicholas teed off at the honorary  starter ceremony joined for the first  time by tom watson  the three champions have a combined 11  green jackets in a few hours all eyes  will be on five time champion tiger  woods he plans his return to tournament  golf just 14 months after he was badly  injured in a car crash cbs sports will  broadcast the masters for the 67th  consecutive year and the great jim nance  of cbs sports will be covering the  masters for the 37th year in a row he  joins us from augusta national jim good  morning my friend how are you doing good  morning good morning friends it's great  to get this all underway it was a  special ceremony just minutes ago we're  in a 30-minute delay because of heavy  rains getting the course prepared and  yes the masters is officially  let's start with tiger woods less than  14 months ago he had this car accident  we remind everybody that he could have  lost his leg it was a car crash he could  have lost his life did you think that  you would see tiger woods back in  tournament play  i did not  i was just with tiger a few weeks ago  down  in jupiter florida where he lives and we  taped a documentary that will air this  sunday on cbs at one o'clock the 25 year  anniversary of his win for the ages and  i got no real indication at all spending  a good portion of the day with tiger  that he'd be ready this soon he did say  he would be playing at some point this  year but  i didn't expect it to be this quickly so  no one works harder i mean it's just  amazing to see the determination that's  still there at 46. and uh i think i  think he's going to play well  we saw his practice round we're looking  at clips of him hitting the ball but  when you were with him you can assess a  athlete's body how did he look how was  he walking around does he look like he's  physically ready for this  well physically i mean he works out like  no one else uh the day i saw him he  began his day at six o'clock with a four  hour workout and i said how did it go  this morning goes um same as it is every  day i hate it i hate every minute of it  but he puts in that work it and  he doesn't let the fact that it's hard  and it's not enjoyable getting away from  the goal and that is to compete and  still try to compete for major  championships but there is a little bit  of a hitch in his uh gate  that would be expected you documented it  nate i mean it was february 23rd a year  ago  and i had just conducted an interview  with him in the tower at riviera in los  angeles  a day and a half before that and and  next thing you know like you said it  could have lost his leg but he truly  could have lost his life it was a  horrific accident one car accident  that  i don't know how he survived it to be  honest but here he is back again he  hasn't competed in a real tournament  he's played in the father-son event with  charlie  his son but he hasn't played in a real  tournament since we had the masters  tournament in the fall of 2020. in  november of 2020 is the last time he put  the t in the ground and competed for  real until today  hey jim you mentioned that hitch in  tigers gate so the the course there in  augusta i think is about more than 7 000  yards if you're a golf ball if you're a  human being walking the whole thing uh  talk to us about the rigors just of that  process  well that i think is his biggest concern  his swing is fine although we'll have to  see when he gets some side hill lies and  has to push off that right leg because  you fire off of that side  and that's going to be demanding now  here here's the thing he came here last  week and got everybody stirred because  he flew into augusta for a practice  round he wanted to see what the recovery  was like for him after that now remember  he's been playing nine whole practice  rounds this week but he's got to play  today tomorrow if he makes the cut  saturday sunday so it builds it gets  gradually more difficult for him and  here's the x factor it's it's wet here  we had three and a half hour three and a  half inches of rain over the last two  days it's soggy we call it being  heavy-legged when you play in conditions  like this and uh that's gonna make it a  little bit more difficult still  this guy just has a way of performing  and i think he's gonna do a lot better  than people think he has one benefit and  that is there are zero expectations for  him to do well  so he comes in here  with us  just in awe of seeing him play again no  one expects him to contend so  from that standpoint mentally i think  it's a good thing i think he's got a  freebie so to speak because the  expectations are so low now don't fool  yourself his expectations are to win  this thing that's all he cares about  he's here to win that's it i hadn't  thought of i haven't thought of it that  way the expectations but i'll bet he has  a lot of self-imposed pressure because  he wants to pull this off but i'm also  curious about other players because i  think everybody's excited to see tiger  including i would think his com his his  competitors but who are the other names  that are going hey fellas you know i'm  here too playing who are those people  that we should also be looking at that's  a good question gayle i will say this i  don't think any of the other players are  saying hey look at me give me some  attention they love the fact that this  tournament as of  monday when he said i think i can play  has been completely about tiger so for  those who are expected to do well they  too benefit by this psychologically  justin thomas john rahm  dustin johnson brooks koepka jordan  spieth and don't forget rory mcilroy who  has now his eighth attempt to complete  the career slam grand slam and golf and  i think he's someone to watch i really  do and he's coming in again not  shouldering the burden of all these  expectations that everybody's going to  heap on him it's all about tigers so  these guys like the fact they're coming  in kind of under the radar to play this  tournament if it's not tiger jim do you  have any predictions on who you think  will be wearing that green jacket on  sunday i was afraid you're going to put  me on the limb i'll go i'm always a  story guy i like what the best story is  we've got a young man named scottie  scheffler who's won three times in the  last six weeks  he's going to be dangerous but i you  know the story of mcilroy trying to  complete the career grand slam um there  have only been six who have ever done it  and and uh  rory this is the one missing piece and i  i would i would love to see rory be the  next guy to win all four legs of of the  major championships  and i know roy would be looking forward  to putting on that green jacket for the  first time right right here that's where  we do it yeah this is this is the  ceremony spot right here  before we let you go i have to ask you  about um how you get this all done you  have been called the busiest person in  all of tv so you go from the final four  to the championship game and now the  masters in the span of seven days how do  you just get your rest between monday  night's championship game and this  morning and this appearance right here  i'm fine i am renewed i'm thrilled to be  here it's the 37th year in a row i've  gone from the ncaa championship game  right into augusta i call it a tradition  unlike any other yes jim nance give  yourself a round of applause  thank you guys all right thank you so  much hi now here's the rundown of all of  the master's action here on cbs today  and tomorrow we'll bring you the  highlights at 11 35 pm third round  coverage begins saturday at 3 p.m  eastern noon pacific and the final round  coverage starts sunday at 2 p.m eastern  11 a.m pacific here on cbs end on our  streaming service paramount plus

